6. Verification and Assurance Claims

A passing producer audit, browser audit, parity result, tamper result, independent
verifier self-test, independent reconstruction result, frozen corpus verification
result, checksum result, or other verification result applies only to the declared
files, profiles, inputs, corpora, rules, manifests, evidence, and verification
boundary associated with that result.

Modified files, changed rules, changed profiles, changed corpora, changed
manifests, changed evidence, changed inputs, or changed verification artifacts
require their own verification.

Redistribution, modification, or use of the covered materials must not imply
third-party verification, certification, production qualification, legal
approval, consent verification, security approval, safety approval, or
endorsement by the original project maintainers unless such a claim has been
separately and expressly authorized.

Producer-side audits, cross-implementation parity checks, and separate
implementation reconstruction do not, by themselves, constitute independent
third-party verification or certification.

